 \r\n \r\n   \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n Hi,&nbsp;\n\n\r\n I&rsquo;m Greg Ip. You might remember me from WSJ&rsquo;s Real Time Economics newsletter. I also write the weekly Capital Account column, which gives you fresh insight into the most fascinating trends in U.S. and global economics.\n\n\r\n Starting next week, I&rsquo;ll be sending you our new and improved WSJ Economics newsletter. Every Tuesday and Thursday, the newsletter will feature my take on a critical issue in finance or economics. I&rsquo;ll draw on my decades of experience as well as the vast reporting resources and expertise of the WSJ economics team. Can you imagine a more vital time? Every day brings a new twist in the world, whether rising global interest rates, another phase of trade war, a challenge from China or an AI breakthrough that could transform work and business. \n\n\r\n I&rsquo;ll also give you quick summaries of the most interesting news, social media, Substacks and academia, plus highlights of the big upcoming events in economics. I know your time is precious, so I promise to be concise. You&rsquo;ll be done in less than five minutes. \n\n\r\n Thanks, and I look forward to staying in touch. Don&rsquo;t hesitate to reach out by replying to this email or writing to me at wsjeconomics@wsj.com . \n\n\r\n &mdash;Greg Ip \n\n\r\n P.S. Subscriptions make our journalism possible. WSJ Economics readers can enjoy a special rate on a new subscription . If you&rsquo;re already a WSJ subscriber, thank you for your support. \n\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n   \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n   \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n Unsubscribe \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n 